  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You call forth a bestial spirit. It appears in an unoccupied space you can see within range and uses the Bestial Spirit stat block. When you cast the spell, choose an environment: Air, Land, or Water. The creature looks like an animal of your choice native to that environment, which determines some details of its stat block. It disappears when it drops to 0 Hit Points or when the spell ends.</p><p><strong>Combat.</strong> The creature is an ally to you and your allies. In combat, it shares your Initiative count but takes its turn immediately after yours. It obeys your verbal commands (no action required by you); if you give none, it takes the Dodge action and uses its movement to avoid danger.</p><p><strong>Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.</strong> Use the spell slot’s level for the spell’s level in the stat block.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-UHZh4KgUMPuGYpkF\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Summon asks for the environment. The spirit’s AC, Hit Points and Rend damage include the spell’s level.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
